    "A": "Under signaling theory, dividend changes convey management's private information about future earnings prospects. An INCREASE signals management confidence that higher earnings are sustainable. A DECREASE, even if motivated by positive investment opportunities, may be interpreted as management signaling that current earnings are insufficient to sustain the dividend — a negative signal about financial health. Westlake should consider maintaining the dividend and funding the expansion through debt or equity issuance to avoid sending a mixed signal.",
    "B": "Under MM dividend irrelevance, investors are indifferent between dividends and capital gains. Cutting the dividend to fund a positive-NPV expansion should have no effect on the stock price because shareholders can create homemade dividends by selling shares.",
