  "ExplanationCorrect": "The maximum acceptable acquisition price is the target's stand-alone value plus the present value of all synergies created by the combination. After-tax synergies = $6.2M × (1 − 0.26) = $4.588M. As a perpetuity, PV(Synergies) = $4.588M / 0.105 = $43.70M. Total acquisition value to Orion = $85M + $43.70M = $128.70M. If Orion pays exactly $128.70M, the NPV of the acquisition to Orion is zero — all synergy value accrues to Vega's shareholders. If Orion pays less than $128.70M (e.g., $100M), Orion shareholders capture part of the synergy value. If Orion pays more than $128.70M, the acquisition destroys value for Orion shareholders. The maximum premium over stand-alone value = $43.70M / $85M = 51.4%. The key insight: synergies determine how much the acquirer CAN pay; competitive dynamics (other bidders) determine how much the acquirer MUST pay. The acquirer's goal is to pay as little as possible above stand-alone value while still winning the deal.",
