  "ExplanationWrongC": "The synergies described — elimination of duplicate facilities and purchasing economies — represent permanent structural cost reductions, not temporary savings. A perpetuity is the appropriate valuation framework for synergies that continue indefinitely. Limiting the horizon to 5 years would understate the synergy value by $26.53M (from $43.70M to $17.17M) and cause Orion to underbid, potentially losing the acquisition to a competitor who correctly values the perpetual synergies. The choice between perpetuity and finite horizon depends on the nature of the synergies — structural cost savings warrant perpetual treatment.",
